hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1476","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Mukhurami told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Basir, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to Medina and met Ubayy Ibn Ka’b, and I said: O Abu Al-Mundhir, tell me the most amazing hadith I have ever heard. From the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He prayed for us or the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the dawn prayer for us, then he turned around and said: Is so-and-so watching?” We said: No, and he did not witness the prayer. He said: “Is so-and-so witnessing?” We said: No, and he did not witness the prayer, so he said: “The heaviest prayers for the hypocrites are the evening prayer and the dawn prayer, and if they knew what is in them, they would have performed them even if Crawling, the row of the presenter is like the row of angels, and if you knew his virtue, you would hasten to him, and your prayer with a man is more terrifying than your prayer. Alone, and your prayer with two men is better than your prayer with one man, and whatever it is more is more beloved to God.” Abu Bakr said: It was narrated by Shu’bah and Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Basir, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, and they did not say about His father"
"1477","Yahya bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Jaafar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Basir He narrates, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, and he said: “Is so-and-so witnessing?” So he mentioned the hadith, and said: “And what “It is more, for it is more beloved to God Almighty.”"
